course: dictionary
lesson: 4470
title: Harmless: looks and meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Harmless means not able to hurt or damage anyone or anything. Read this: «Most bacteria are harmless or even helpful, but some bacteria and viruses get into the body and make us ill.» The word but is a clue. It tells you that the first part is the good news, and the second part is the bad news. So harmless bacteria cannot make you ill.
explain: Looks can fool you. Some creatures look scary but are harmless, like most spiders in the UK. Others look harmless but are dangerous. That is why you should never touch a wild animal or plant you do not know, even if it looks friendly.
explain: Harmless can also describe fun and jokes. «Harmless fun» means fun that does not upset or hurt anyone. Swap the word into the sentence to check: if the joke makes someone cry, it is not harmless fun, however funny it seemed to the teller.
fact: «Harmless» means not able to hurt or damage anyone or anything.
fact: «Harmless» can also mean not meant to upset anyone, as in «harmless fun».
fact: «Harmlessly» is the adverb: it describes how something is done without causing damage.
fact: «Most bacteria are harmless or even helpful», and your gut holds trillions of useful ones.
fact: A joke is harmless only if nobody is hurt or upset.
exercise: «Most bacteria are harmless or even helpful.» What does harmless mean here? | *Not able to hurt or damage anyone or anything | Hidden under the ground | Very large and dangerous | Loud and noisy
exercise: Jamal says, «It was only harmless fun, nobody got hurt.» What does harmless fun mean? | Fun that is very dangerous | *A joke that does not hurt or upset anyone | Fun that needs a helmet | Silly fun that makes everyone cry
exercise: A grass snake looks scary, but what does it mean if it is harmless? | It is very hungry | *It cannot hurt you | It runs very fast | It is wet and cold
test: In «Most bacteria are harmless or even helpful, but some bacteria and viruses get into the body and make us ill», which word shows the contrast between the good news and the bad news? | Body | Bacteria | *But | Harmless
test: Which word is the adverb form of harmless? | Harmful | Harm | *Harmlessly | Harmless fun
exam: Scary-looking creatures can be harmless, so what should you do with a wild plant or animal you don't know? | *Don't touch it | Pick it up to look closer | Take it home | Give it a name
